CHAPTER.VERS:
Truly, truly, I say to you

          {+}
        , He who does not enter by the door into the fold of the sheep, but climbs up some other way, the same is a thief and a robber.

Jesus therefore said again, Truly, truly, I say to you

          {+}
        , I am the door of the sheep.

And many of them said, He has a demon, and is insane; why do you

          {+}
         hear him?

Jesus answered them, I told you

          {+}
        , and you

          {+}
         do not believe: the works that I do in my Father's name, these bear witness of me.

But you

          {+}
         do not believe, because you

          {+}
         are not of my sheep.

Jesus answered them, Many good works I have shown you

          {+}
         from the Father; for which of those works do you

          {+}
         stone me?

Jesus answered them, Is it not written in your

          {+}
         law, I said, you

          {+}
         are gods?

do you

          {+}
         say of him, whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world, You blaspheme; because I said, I am [the] Son of God?

But if I do them, though you

          {+}
         don't believe me, believe the works: that you

          {+}
         may know and understand that the Father is in me, and I in the Father.
